  "title": "The app catalog had a growth spurt",
  "summary": "The app catalog grew rapidly while scoped keys, account APIs, and new models gave those apps more ways to work with Pollinations.\n\nCommunity listings arrived across creative tools, chat clients, classroom projects, games, bots, and developer workflows. The catalog and README showcase were updated to make more of them discoverable. These are listings of community projects, not newly added Pollinations API features.\n\nKey creation and authorization now share controls for allowed models, Pollen budgets, expiry, and account permissions. Apps can preselect those options, and permitted keys can request profile, balance, and usage data. The authorization page and API docs now explain what access a key grants.\n\nFLUX.2 [klein] 4B was added for image generation and reference-based editing, and the community-built `nomnom` joined in Alpha for web search, scraping, and crawling. Claude and Claude Large gained a fallback from Bedrock to Vertex AI, while DeepSeek V3.2 moved to Fireworks AI. Existing aliases were retained.\n\nPlay added audio generation, model-specific voice choices, and playback. Its output stays visible when switching models. Community contributor CloudCompile added Bring Your Own Pollen to chat.pollinations.ai, so people can connect their own key for model listings and chat, image, and video requests, then disconnect to return to the default key.",
  "pr_count": 140,
